    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0965" n="831" xml:id="pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860b.00/7–1145</note>
                <head>No. 556<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Southern
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Huston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Mr. Walworth Barbour, of the Division of Southern
                        European Affairs</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-11">July 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Frangeš called yesterday and brought up the following:</p>
                <p>1. A memorandum which he said CWC<anchor n="1" xml:id="d556-f1"/> had asked for.
                    I have sent a copy to CWC.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">loyce</hi>] K H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">uston</hi>] </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d556-a1.xml" xpointer="d556-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="1" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>Cavendish W. Cannon, a member of the United States Delegation at the Berlin
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
